    "PREAMBLE": "Bijoy Das @ Bijay Das vs Unknown on 12 June, 2024\nAuthor: Arijit Banerjee Bench: Arijit Banerjee 12.06.2024 Item no. 19.\nCourt No.28.\nAB (Rejected) CRM (DB) 1692 of 2024 In Re: An Application for Bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure in connection with Nandakumar Police Station Case No.26 of 2024 Dated 11.1.2024 under Sections 376/354C of the Indian Penal Code read with Section 67/67A of the IT Act\nAnd In the matter of : Bijoy Das @ Bijay Das ......Petitioner.\nMr. Navanil De, Ms. Monami Mukherjee ......for the Petitioner.\nMr. Sanjay Bardhan, Mr. Aritra Bhattacharya......for the State.\nSigned By :\nAPURBA BANDYOPADHYAY High Court of Calcutta 13 th of June 2024 06:22:42 PM\n",
    "facts": "The charge against the petitioner is under Sections 376/354C IPC read with Sections 67/67A of the Information Technology (Amendment) Act, 2008.\nThe prosecution case is that the victim lady became friends with the petitioner after coming in contact with him on face book.\nThe petitioner used to reside close to the residence of the victim.\nOne day, taking advantage of the absence of the victim's husband, the petitioner went to her and offered her some Prasad.\nAfter consuming the Prasad she felt dizzy.\nThe petitioner took indecent pictures of the victim lady and threatened to circulate the same in the social media.\nHe is in custody for 144 days.\n",
